Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add desktop-selected model routing and Gemini base URL

Reason: Finoka's desktop settings can select one preferred model globally and
override it for individual LLM task groups. FineSub already owns the model
catalog and route planner, so the desktop writes target IDs into the shared
llm config and this patch composes those preferences with the packaged preset.

An API provider's selected target leads the existing group instead of replacing
it: custom OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic transports are text-only, and keeping
the packaged candidates behind them preserves a media-capable fallback for audio
and video tasks. A selected **local CLI** keeps no such tail. It runs on the
user's own subscription, so continuing on Gemini is not a fallback they asked
for -- and when no Gemini key is configured the chain walks off the end and
reports `Provider GEMINI_PAID is disabled or has no selected API key`, which is
about a tier nobody chose and says nothing about what the CLI did. Packaged
members on the same provider tier stay, because they are the same CLI: that is
what keeps agy's search-declaring twin reachable for a `retrieval=native` call.
A task the selected CLI cannot serve now fails its capability check up front,
naming the CLI and the capability it lacks, instead of silently changing model.

Gemini's REST transport also needs to honor the Base URL saved by the same
settings panel.

Removal: Delete once upstream exposes an equivalent preferred-target overlay
and reads GEMINI_BASE_URL for direct REST calls.

